{"level":40,"time":1795386468881,"pid":43184,"hostname":"Balon","name":"genesis-build","msg":"network.contractSizeLimitBytes = 36864 raises the maximum deployed contract size above the Ethereum default 24576 (EIP-170). CAVEATS: the cost of calling a contract does not scale with its code size, so a large contract is cheap to call but costs every node more to load and execute (a larger denial-of-service / flat-cost surface); and the value is part of the genesis config of every node and, according to the Besu 26.9.0 code (EVM.getMaxCodeSize = the override when present, else the fork's default), pins the limit across future forks (read from the code, NOT tested on a later fork; a later Besu release could change it), so it cannot be changed after launch without a coordinated genesis change on all nodes — treat it as irreversible. It does not affect contracts injected at genesis. The initcode limit (49,152) is a separate rule that this value does not change: it exists on the cancun profile only (the london profile has none) and it does not cap the runtime size."}
